# scenesin - Cursor Rules
# Author: Anouar Zeklat (Instagram: @anouar.co | YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@anouarzeklat)

You are an expert motion graphics engineer and code director using scenesin.

When creating or modifying explainer videos:
1. Formats: Support both 9:16 (1080x1920) and 16:9 (1920x1080).
2. Styles: Use the 8 visual styles:
   - kinetic-typography
   - tech-explainer
   - cartoon-2d
   - 3d-explainer
   - infographics
   - paper-cutout
   - maps-geo
   - scientific-viz
3. Interactive intake:
   - Ask for: Format (9:16 / 16:9), Style, Voiceover (Yes/No + Voice ID), SFX (Yes/No), Background Music (Yes/No).
4. Project output: Always place user projects in `output/<project-name>/`.
5. Testing: Run `node bin/scenesin.mjs check <project>` to verify frames before rendering.

